{#- Atlas — surface one: feature planning on a desk (decisions 22, 23, 24, 25, and #780).

  NOT A TABLE. M1 built this page as an HTML table — features as columns, ladder rows as `<tr>`,
  every intersection a `<td>` — and every visual complaint in #780 followed from that. Cells want
  borders and labels and equal weight, so the arrow became a glyph in a box, finished work became a
  fill with the word "Passed" in it, and future work needed something in it because a cell looks
  broken when it is empty. The owner's framing, and it sat above everything else on the list: it is
  not a chart and they are not grid cells.

  What it is instead: one ribbon per feature descending a shared ladder. The ladder supplies the
  vertical scale; the ribbons are the drawing. Nothing occupies a cell, because there are no cells.

  THIS LAYOUT POSITIONS NOTHING. Every coordinate and every path comes from `src/chart.mjs`, which
  is pure and unit-tested; this file interpolates them. That is the same rule M1's version followed
  for the two ends of a column, applied to the whole picture — a layout that computes a position is
  a layout no test without a browser can check, and there is no browser here.

  Two drawings, side by side inside one horizontal scroller:

    * the LADDER gutter, which is `position: sticky; left: 0` so it stays put while
    * the LANES scroll sideways under it.

  A lane is drawn about its own origin and placed with a single `transform`, so `theme/order.js`
  can move a whole feature — ribbon, dots, dates, skip marker and balloon together — by rewriting
  one number, with no geometry on the client at all.

  Data this layout expects:
    chart — computeChart(ladder, workstreams)'s output: rows, bands, rules and lanes
    project, repo, title — see base.njk
-#}
{% extends "base.njk" %}
{% import "base.njk" as ui %}

{% block bodyClass %}page page-planning{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<h1>Feature planning</h1>
<p class="lede">One ribbon per feature, from the top of the ladder through the stages and on into the milestones. A solid arrow covers what has begun; where more is on record than has been started, a second, fainter arrow reaches as far as the records go. Both end in their own head.</p>

<div class="chart-scroll" data-planning-scroll>
<svg class="planning-ladder" width="{{ chart.ladderWidth }}" height="{{ chart.height }}" viewBox="0 0 {{ chart.ladderWidth }} {{ chart.height }}" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
<rect class="ladder-ground" x="0" y="0" width="{{ chart.ladderWidth }}" height="{{ chart.height }}"/>
{%- for band in chart.bands %}{% if band.id == "execution" %}
{%- set mid = (band.y + band.height / 2) | round -%}
<text class="band-name" x="18" y="{{ mid }}" transform="rotate(-90 18 {{ mid }})" text-anchor="middle">{{ band.label }}</text>
{%- endif %}{% endfor %}
{%- for row in chart.rows %}
<text class="{% if row.kind == "stage" %}lad-stage{% else %}lad-num num{% endif %}" x="{{ chart.ladderWidth - 14 }}" y="{{ row.centre + 4 }}" text-anchor="end">{{ row.caption }}</text>
{%- endfor %}
<line class="ladder-edge" x1="{{ chart.ladderWidth }}" y1="0" x2="{{ chart.ladderWidth }}" y2="{{ chart.ladderBottom }}"/>
</svg>

<svg class="planning-chart" width="{{ chart.lanesWidth }}" height="{{ chart.height }}" viewBox="0 0 {{ chart.lanesWidth }} {{ chart.height }}" data-planning-chart data-column-pitch="{{ chart.columnPitch }}" role="group" aria-label="One ribbon per feature down a shared ladder of stages and milestones. Every feature is also listed in full on the triage view.">
<defs>
<filter id="balloon-shadow" x="-30%" y="-40%" width="160%" height="200%"><feDropShadow dx="0" dy="3" stdDeviation="4" flood-color="#0f172a" flood-opacity="0.16"/></filter>
</defs>

{#- The four bands (#780). They belong to the ladder rather than to any feature, so the phase reads
    horizontally across every feature at once — the horizontal reading is the phase, the vertical
    is the individual feature's path. -#}
<g class="bands">
{%- for band in chart.bands %}
<rect class="band band-{{ band.id }}" x="0" y="{{ band.y }}" width="{{ chart.lanesWidth }}" height="{{ band.height }}"/>
{%- endfor %}
</g>

{#- A light rule at every ladder row, drawn BENEATH the ribbons, so a ribbon crosses a rule rather
    than being cut by it. Lines, not a grid: the moment these meet verticals they are cells again. -#}
<g class="rules">
{%- for y in chart.rules %}
<line class="rule" x1="0" y1="{{ y }}" x2="{{ chart.lanesWidth }}" y2="{{ y }}"/>
{%- endfor %}
</g>

<g class="lanes" data-lanes>
{%- for lane in chart.lanes %}
<g class="lane" data-slug="{{ lane.slug }}" transform="translate({{ lane.x }},0)">

<g class="lane-head" data-lane-head>
<rect class="lane-head-box" x="4" y="6" width="{{ chart.columnPitch - 16 }}" height="44" rx="8" ry="8"/>
<rect class="lane-head-accent" x="4" y="6" width="5" height="44" rx="2" ry="2"/>
<a href="{{ lane.url }}"><text class="col-h" x="18" y="26">{{ lane.codename }}</text></a>
{{ ui.svgChip("stage", lane.stage, 18, 32) }}
</g>

{#- The ribbon. One object per feature, drawn in two weights: solid over what has begun, faint over
    what is on record beyond it. Each arrow ends in its own head, growing straight out of its own
    body — nothing floats, and there is never a gap between the two. -#}
<g class="ribbon">
{%- for segment in lane.solid.segments %}
<rect class="ribbon-body tone-{{ segment.tone }}" x="{{ lane.centre - 18 }}" y="{{ segment.y }}" width="{{ lane.solid.width }}" height="{{ segment.height }}" rx="6" ry="6"/>
{%- endfor %}
{%- for d in lane.solid.detours %}
<path class="ribbon-detour" d="{{ d }}" fill="none"/>
{%- endfor %}
<path class="ribbon-head tone-{{ lane.solid.head.tone }}" d="{{ lane.solid.head.d }}"/>
{%- if lane.faint %}
{%- for segment in lane.faint.segments %}
<rect class="ribbon-body tone-{{ segment.tone }}" x="{{ lane.centre - 14 }}" y="{{ segment.y }}" width="{{ lane.faint.width }}" height="{{ segment.height }}" rx="5" ry="5"/>
{%- endfor %}
<path class="ribbon-head tone-{{ lane.faint.head.tone }}" d="{{ lane.faint.head.d }}"/>
{%- endif %}
</g>

{#- A dot per milestone the ribbon covers, with its stored days beside it. Nothing below the final
    arrowhead, whatever its status — the rule is positional, not status-based (#780). -#}
{%- for dot in lane.dots %}
<g class="milestone-dot tone-{{ dot.tone }}">
<circle class="dot{% if dot.hollow %} dot-hollow{% endif %}" cx="{{ lane.centre }}" cy="{{ dot.y }}" r="7"/>
{%- for line in dot.lines %}
<text class="{% if line.strong %}dt-b num{% else %}dt{% endif %}" x="62" y="{{ dot.y - 3 + loop.index0 * 13 }}">{{ line.text }}</text>
{%- endfor %}
</g>
{%- endfor %}

{#- A skipped milestone is noted, not treated as a wall. The ribbon has already left its lane
    around this marker; here is the marker, and the reason to read it at. -#}
{%- for skip in lane.skips %}
<g class="skip-mark">
<circle class="skip-ring" cx="{{ lane.centre }}" cy="{{ skip.y }}" r="12"/>
<path class="skip-cross" d="{{ skip.cross }}" fill="none"/>
<text class="skip-t" x="62" y="{{ skip.y - 3 }}">{{ skip.label }}</text>
<text class="dt" x="62" y="{{ skip.y + 10 }}">{{ skip.reason }}</text>
</g>
{%- endfor %}

{#- The balloon, at the step it describes rather than at the end of the arrow. Fixed width tied to
    the column, growing downward as the text needs; its connector steps into a lane just clear of
    this feature's own ribbon and travels vertically inside this column, so it cannot cross a
    neighbour. No next step, no balloon. -#}
{%- if lane.balloon %}
<g class="balloon tone-{{ lane.balloon.tone }}">
<path class="balloon-line" d="{{ lane.balloon.connector }}" fill="none"/>
<circle class="balloon-pin" cx="{{ lane.balloon.dot.x }}" cy="{{ lane.balloon.dot.y }}" r="4"/>
<path class="balloon-body" d="{{ lane.balloon.path }}" filter="url(#balloon-shadow)"/>
<text class="bl-k" x="{{ lane.balloon.textX }}" y="{{ lane.balloon.kickerY }}">{{ lane.balloon.kicker }}</text>
{%- for line in lane.balloon.lines %}
<text class="bl-t" x="{{ lane.balloon.textX }}" y="{{ line.y }}">{{ line.text }}</text>
{%- endfor %}
</g>
{%- endif %}

</g>
{%- endfor %}
</g>
</svg>
</div>

<ul class="chart-key">
<li><span class="key-swatch tone-done"></span>finished</li>
<li><span class="key-swatch tone-live"></span>in progress</li>
<li><span class="key-swatch tone-ahead"></span>on record, not started</li>
<li><span class="key-swatch key-skip"></span>skipped — the work went round it</li>
</ul>
{% endblock %}
